mo precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No se puede asumir que haya actos maliciosos sin comprobar los motivos reales.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o fechas específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 87 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 17.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 6.9. December accounts for 17% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. The number of contracts does not prove misconduct, as market prices or budget constraints may influence spending decisions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts awarded in December to see if they align with seasonal needs. Review the awardee A's contracts to determine if they repeat the same service or product. Analyze if multiple contracts cover the same need to assess potential duplication or inefficiency.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["nbVKvOs%2BYWDs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","dR%2BNVRtSlA4Xhk1FZxEyvw%3D%3D","%2BXMwpwVGj2CopEMYCmrbmw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}